for n,a,b in [(12,'good impulses still live','the immediate force of truth still lives'),(22,'Before the month was out he would have taken out the last note but one, feeling that returning even a single hundred would serve, since a thief would have stolen the lot.','Before the month was out he would have taken out the last hundred but one, thinking: “If I return even one hundred, it comes to the same thing: a scoundrel, but not a thief. I have squandered twenty-nine hundreds, but returned one; a thief would not have returned even that.”')]:
 t=c['paragraphs'][n-1]
